-- title:
--   Counting Frobⁿ-fixed places of the modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $\ell$, let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $n$ be a natural number with $0 < n$. Write $F_N(k) = \mathrm{ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,k\,N$ for the intermediate field of $k((q))$ over $k$ generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k\,d\,(\mathrm{jqModC}\,k)$, i.e. the $q$-expansions $\bar j(q^d)$, as $d$ runs over the nonzero divisors of $N$. A place of a field extension $F/k$ here means a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $k$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; its degree is the $k$-dimension of its residue field. The map [`ModularCurve.frobeniusPlaceModL K N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_FrobeniusModL.html#L172) sends a place $w$ of $F_N(K)/K$ to its restriction along the $K$-algebra endomorphism $\mathrm{frobeniusModL}$ of $F_N(K)$ given on $q$-expansions by $f(q) \mapsto f(q^{\ell})$. The assertion is that the set of fixed points of the $n$-th iterate of this map is finite, and that its cardinality equals the cardinality of the set of places of degree one of $F_N(\mathbb{F}_{\ell^n})$ over $\mathbb{F}_{\ell^n} = \mathrm{GaloisField}\ \ell\ n$.
--
--   Both numbers count the $\mathbb{F}_{\ell^n}$-rational points of the modular curve of level $N$ in characteristic $\ell$: the left-hand side as the geometric points fixed by the $n$-th power of the geometric Frobenius on the function field over an algebraically closed base, the right-hand side as the rational places of the corresponding function field over the finite field $\mathbb{F}_{\ell^n}$. It is used in the constructions of glued specialisations and of inertia-fixed classes in the degree-zero Picard group, where a supply of Frobenius-fixed places of prescribed finite number is needed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finite_fixedPoints_frobeniusPlaceModL_iterate_and_card_eq.lean

import Mathlib
